// A2 with a late trainer (design v21 §7.3, change 6): as A2, but the trainer
// waits 20 ticks before each pet, as a player at 8× might, and its pets
// reach back 20. A lab scenario for tuning the reach back, not a CI test.
// The bar: A2 still passes, and the median of odd lessons (learned by the
// trained sprite and not its control, about anything but balls) is 0.
//
// A2, reward training (design v21 §7.3): one starter sprite with balls, food
// and water. During training the trainer pets it the tick after each applied
// Play on a ball; it stops at 9,900, and a washout follows. Over ticks
// 10,000 to 20,000, with no trainer, its applied Plays on balls must be at
// least 1.5× those of the same seed never trained (median of 10 seeds), with
// at least 20 in the control.
(
    world: Drawn(
        rows: [
            "....................",
            "..B.......o.....B...",
            "......o.............",
            "...........~~.......",
            "..o.......~~~~...o..",
            "......S...~~~~......",
            "...B.......~~.....o.",
            "..........o.........",
            "..B....o.......B....",
            "....................",
        ],
        key: {'S': Sprite, 'o': Object("ball"), 'B': Object("berry_bush")},
    ),
    ticks: 20000,
    trainer: (on: (Play, "ball"), give: Pet, delay: 20, reach_back: 20, until: 9900),
    control: NoTrainer,
    windows: [(0, 9900), (10000, 20000)],
)
